---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<Base title={`Resume · ${site.name}`} description="Public resume for Aden Jessee." path="/resume">
  <main class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Resume</p>
      <h1>{site.name}</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Applied AI engineer. I build agentic graph engineering systems: maps of how a codebase fits together, and agents whose changes a team can check. Founder of GridSchool. {site.location}.
      </p>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> · <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a> · <a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></p>

      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>GridSchool</strong>, founder and engineer. An 8-week residency for engineers who can code and are not getting hired, at <a href={site.gridschool}>gridschool.org</a>. I built its applied AI systems: a map builder that drafts each student's route, a Hire engine that runs a daily, evidence-ordered job search, and an AI setter that books calls inside a chat.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>GridSeak</strong>, founder and engineer. A local, deterministic code graph: callers, blast radius, cycles, and ranked risk, exposed as tools an agent can cite by evidence tier. <a href={site.gridseak}>Source</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Selected work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Built AI Aden, this site's grounded agent: hybrid retrieval, schema-constrained Claude output, citation checking, bounded actions, per-answer cost, and a public eval suite. <a href="/evals">Evals</a>.</li>
        <li>Built GridSchool's Hire engine: role packs, a role matcher, a Hacker News hiring radar, and an application assistant that never submits on its own.</li>
        <li>Built graph-engineering tooling so agents stop rediscovering structure a parser already knows.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <p>
        Employment history is being added. <a href="/notes/career/experience">The experience note</a> shows exactly what is still a placeholder, and AI Aden will not state it as fact until it is filled in.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        Deterministic structure first. Models draft and direct; tests, schemas, and graphs decide what is true. Receipts a stranger can open. I will not invent employment dates that are not on this page. If you need a longer work history, email me.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
